  "id": "matching-familiar-figures-test",
  "term": "Matching Familiar Figures Test",
  "definition": "The Matching Familiar Figures Test is a learning-related measure used to assess how quickly and accurately a person responds when choosing among alternatives. In this context, its response latency and error rate are used as indicators of conceptual tempo, distinguishing more impulsive fast-but-error-prone responding from more reflective slower-and-more-accurate responding.",
